# JaCoCo: class excludes and failing thresholds

JaCoCo cannot ignore a source line range. Do not use `SOURCE`-retention `@Generated` as an ignore (it never reaches bytecode). Exclude a **class** only when tests must not run it:

- Thin vendor SDK wrappers (and their client producers) that tests **mock** and must not call.
- Process lifecycle that only runs outside the test launch mode (one-shot job `run` then process exit).

Use the **same** class set for the HTML/XML report and for `jacocoTestCoverageVerification`. A missing resource (`get == null`) is not an API failure; do not catch a vendor exception and return `false` solely to paint a catch line green, and do not mock a client the project forbids mocking just to hit that catch.

**Fail the build** when covered ratio is below: instructions **0.80**, lines **1.00**, branches **0.70**. Wire `check` (and `test`) to `jacocoTestCoverageVerification`. Thresholds live in `gradle.properties`. If tests run under a Quarkus classloader, write the Quarkus exec file and exclude `*QuarkusClassLoader` from the JUnit agent; do not treat a framework HTML report as the gate if it ignores these excludes.

```properties
# gradle.properties
jacoco.minimum.instruction=0.80
jacoco.minimum.line=1.00
jacoco.minimum.branch=0.70
```

```properties
# application.properties — Gradle is the gate; skip a second HTML report that ignores excludes
quarkus.jacoco.report=false
```

```kotlin
val jacocoMainClasses =
    layout.buildDirectory.dir("classes/kotlin/main").map { dir ->
        fileTree(dir) {
            exclude("**/VendorSdkAdapter*")
            exclude("**/VendorClientProducer*")
            exclude("**/JobLifecycleObserver*")
        }
    }

tasks.withType<JacocoReportBase>().configureEach {
    classDirectories.setFrom(jacocoMainClasses)
}

tasks.jacocoTestCoverageVerification {
    violationRules {
        rule {
            limit {
                counter = "INSTRUCTION"
                minimum = providers.gradleProperty("jacoco.minimum.instruction").get().toBigDecimal()
            }
            limit {
                counter = "LINE"
                minimum = providers.gradleProperty("jacoco.minimum.line").get().toBigDecimal()
            }
            limit {
                counter = "BRANCH"
                minimum = providers.gradleProperty("jacoco.minimum.branch").get().toBigDecimal()
            }
        }
    }
}

tasks.test { finalizedBy(tasks.jacocoTestReport, tasks.jacocoTestCoverageVerification) }
tasks.check { dependsOn(tasks.jacocoTestCoverageVerification) }
```
